{
  "info": {
    "name": "Gateway (Team 14) - Guild and Package Registry",
    "description": "The API gateway, and Guild Service and Package Registry Service reached through it.\n\nOwner: IsStephy. Gateway port: 8080.\n\nNeeds the shared stack with the gateway, User Management, Guild and Package Registry running, and the same GATEWAY_KEY on the gateway and both services. Players register and log in through the gateway (User Management issues real RS256 tokens); the gateway verifies each token, strips Authorization and forwards the verified user as X-User-Id.\n\nRe-runnable: usernames carry {{$timestamp}}.\n\nPackage Registry's admin-only success paths are not here: admins are seeded by user id (PACKAGE_REGISTRY_INITIAL_ADMIN_USER_ID), and User Management issues fresh UUIDs per run. They are covered by collections/package-registry-service.postman_collection.json against the service on its own.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "gatewayUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080"
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": "Gateway-test-123"
    },
    {
      "key": "monsterRaidServiceKey",
      "value": "change_me"
    },
    {
      "key": "runId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "ownerId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "ownerToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "memberId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "memberToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "inviteeId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "inviteeToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "guildId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "chatUrl",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Gateway",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Gateway Health",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// A fresh id per run keeps usernames unique, so the collection is re-runnable.",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('runId', pm.variables.replaceIn('{{$timestamp}}'));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "pm.test('it is the gateway', function () { pm.expect(pm.response.json().service).to.eql('gateway'); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gatewayUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{gatewayUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The gateway's own liveness check."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Guild and Package Registry are reachable",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const services = pm.response.json().services;",
                  "pm.test('guild-service is up behind the gateway', function () { pm.expect(services['guild-service'].status).to.eql('ok'); });",
                  "pm.test('package-registry-service is up behind the gateway', function () { pm.expect(services['package-registry-service'].status).to.eql('ok'); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gatewayUrl}}/health/services",
              "host": [
                "{{gatewayUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health",
                "services"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The gateway polls every service's /health. This collection only checks Guild and Package Registry, so the status code (200, or 503 while another service is down) is not asserted."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
